<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">May Thirtieth Movement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1925">1925</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The May Thirtieth Movement was a wave of anti-imperialist strikes and protests in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> that followed the shooting of demonstrators by the International Settlement's police on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a> Road, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanghai">Shanghai</a>, on 30 May 1925. Strikes and boycotts of British and Japanese goods spread to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangzhou">Canton</a> and other cities. The movement greatly strengthened the Nationalist and Communist parties.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/may-thirtieth-movement.jpg" alt="May Thirtieth Movement" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:May_30th_Movement_Propaganda_Poster.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
